From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 17:11:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Propagate damage through shadow roots

propagate_damage_flags bailed on any node without stylo_element_data. A
shadow root has none, so the walk returned before traversing the shadow
subtree: box-construction damage and layout-cache clears for content
inside a shadow tree never ran, and the nodes could not get boxes no
matter what damage they carried. caniuse renders every feature card into
ciu-feature-list's shadow tree, so search results stopped painting once
incremental layout landed.

Handle a shadow root before the element-only damage processing: it
returns the union of its children's damage, so construction damage
bubbles through it to the flat-tree host without reading element-only
fields.
---
 src/layout/damage.rs | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/layout/damage.rs b/src/layout/damage.rs
index 6485ad8..671622c 100644
--- a/src/layout/damage.rs
+++ b/src/layout/damage.rs
@@ -54,6 +54,19 @@ impl BaseDocument {
     /// without revisiting their DOM children. Damage inside an anonymous box
     /// also invalidates its cache by walking `layout_parent` upward.
     pub(crate) fn propagate_damage_flags(&mut self, node_id: NodeId) -> RestyleDamage {
+        // Shadow roots are transparent flat-tree boundaries, not layout nodes.
+        // Walk their real children and bubble that damage to the host without
+        // touching the element-only layout accessors.
+        if self.nodes[node_id].is_shadow_root() {
+            let children = std::mem::take(&mut self.nodes[node_id].children);
+            let mut damage = RestyleDamage::empty();
+            for child in children.iter() {
+                damage |= self.propagate_damage_flags(*child);
+            }
+            self.nodes[node_id].children = children;
+            return damage;
+        }
+
         let own_damage = if let Some(data) = self.nodes[node_id]
             .try_stylo_element_data_mut()
             .and_then(|s| s.get_mut())
